.TH RC 1
.SH NAME
rc \- command language (in progress - foundation only, no shell yet)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rc
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Rc
is a real translation of Plan 9's
.IR rc (1),
from
.B utils/rcsh/
in this tree - not a workalike. It is being built incrementally; see
.B doc/plan9-terminal-plan.md
for why (a real
.I rc
is what
.IR mk (1)
needs to run genuine Plan 9 mkfile recipes) and for the finding that
changed this translation's shape before it started:
.B utils/rcsh
was never a portable
.IR rc .
Its own mkfile refuses to build for anything but Windows NT/95 -
.B Nt.c
is the only platform binding ever written, and no Posix binding ever
existed here. So this translation is really two different kinds of
work: a real, portable
.I rc
language core (lexer, grammar, word lists, variables, the code-vector
execution engine) to translate directly from
.BR utils/rcsh 's
own source, and an entirely new platform layer (process spawn/wait,
pipes) to design against Limbo's
.B spawn
and channel model from scratch, since there is no Posix reference to
translate that part from.
.PP
This version implements two slices, both with no parser or execution
engine yet - see BUGS. The first is word lists and the variable/
keyword tables from
.B word.c
and
.BR var.c .
The second is
.BR glob.c 's
pure pattern-matching logic
.RI ( deglob ,
.IR match ,
.IR matchfn ,
and a reduced
.I haswild
standing in for
.BR globsize 's
buffer-sizing side effect, which Limbo strings don't need) plus
.BR word.c 's
.IR subwords ,
deferred from the first slice because it needs
.BR deglob .
.BR glob.c 's
directory-walking half
.RI ( globdir ,
.IR glob ,
.IR globsort ,
.IR globlist )
stays deferred - it needs a real argument stack and real directory
reads, the same boundary the first slice's deferred
.IR pushword / popword / pushlist / poplist
already are.
.B Running
.B rc
does nothing but populate its internal tables and print a note saying
so; there is no shell to use yet.
.SH FILES
.B utils/rcsh/
in this tree - the real source being translated.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/rc.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mk (1),
.B doc/plan9-terminal-plan.md
in this tree - the sizing and sequencing document this translation
follows.
.SH BUGS
No lexer, grammar, or execution engine yet - both slices built so far
were chosen specifically because they have real, testable value
semantics without needing any of those (a lexer alone cannot be tested
meaningfully, since real
.IR rc 's
own lexer and grammar are not independent of each other: yacc generates
the token constants the lexer returns).
.PP
.B match() 's
real source manually decodes UTF-8 byte sequences itself, because C's
.B char*
has no idea what a multi-byte code point is. Limbo's
.B string
type already is a rune sequence, so this translation indexes strings
directly instead - a real simplification, not a mechanical translation,
noted in
.BR rc.b 's
own header comment.
.PP
.BR match() 's
.B [...]
bracket-class case has one deliberate behavioral divergence from the
real source: a pattern that runs out before its closing
.B ]
returns 0 (no match) here, where the real source would read past its
own string's NUL terminator - undefined behavior in C, but a Limbo
array-bounds crash if translated as-is, since Limbo strings check
every index at runtime. Only a malformed pattern is affected; a
well-formed one behaves identically.
.PP
Real
.I rc
frees
.BR Word / List / Var / Redir
cells explicitly throughout the source translated so far. Limbo has a
real garbage collector; every one of those free paths is simply
omitted, not translated - stated once here rather than at each
omission.
.PP
.B vlook
in the real source consults the currently running thread's local
variables before falling back to the global table. There is no
Thread yet, so this version's
.B vlook
always falls back to the global table - correct once there is
exactly one, implicit scope (true right now, since nothing here can
create a local variable yet), and due to change once
.B code.c
and
.B exec.c
introduce a real running thread with real local scopes.
